# Gnosis Trademark and Naming Policy

Copyright © 2026 Mikhail Kucheriavyi. All rights reserved.

## Canonical project names

Current product-facing materials use **Gnosis** and **Gnosis Core**. Repository and component names must describe current, evidenced roles. Legacy research codenames and historical release labels are not current product names and should not be used in new product-facing documentation.

## Accurate identification

Project names may be used to identify the official Gnosis project or accurately describe research involving it. Such use must not falsely imply endorsement, certification, sponsorship, partnership, employment, institutional affiliation, or authorization.

A modified, forked, derivative, or independently operated implementation must not be presented as an official Gnosis release unless expressly authorized. Where useful, identify the original version, modifications, and independent maintainer.

## Commercial use

A software license does not automatically grant trademark rights. Commercial use of project names, logos, or visual identity may require separate authorization. Software licensing and trademark authorization are separate matters.

## Legal scope

This policy describes project naming intent. It does not by itself establish a registered trademark in any jurisdiction. Any rights are governed by applicable law.
